  "description": "These spectacularly creamy overnight oats take all of five minutes to prep, and are lightly sweetened with maple syrup and vanilla.",
  "notes": "Total time, including resting: 8 hr 5 min.\n\nOptional or for serving: 1 teaspoon vanilla paste or extract (optional); Fruit, for serving (optional)\n\nNotes: Your choice of dairy or dairy-free milk can be substituted for oat milk. I tested this with regular sweetened oat milk, but if you’d like to cut down on the sugar, you can use unsweetened oat milk. To make gluten-free overnight oats, use gluten-free rolled oats.\n\nMake-ahead and storage: The recipe can easily be doubled. Overnight oats can be refrigerated in an airtight container for up to 3 days.",
